        "text": "An if statement can be used to execute different code blocks based on the role of the current user (admin, moderator, guest).",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "A switch statement can be used as an alternative to if statements for role‑based branching, requiring case clauses for each role and an optional default clause.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Each case clause in a switch statement should end with a break statement to exit the switch block after executing its code.",
        "refs": ["Q0002", "Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "If a break statement is omitted from a case that is not the last one, execution will fall through to the next case.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Switch statements can operate on integer types (byte, short, int) as well as strings; using a string variable as the switch expression without proper handling can cause a compilation error.",
